      "VAMLIN - LF\n(Vesicular Arbuscular Mycorrhiza)\nVAM is a beneficial Symbiotic fungus that\nattaches to plant roots, signiticanty enhancing\nnutrient uptake especially P, Zn, Fe, Cu, water\nabsorption and stress tolerance.\nBenefits:\n• Enhances uptake of phosphorus,\npotassium and micronutrients (Zn, Fe,\nCu).Promotes deeper root systems,\nfaster growth, and better flowers in\nplants.\n• Helps plants withstand environmental\nstresses like drought, salinity, and\ndiseases.\n• The fungus penetrates root cortical\ncells to form arbuscules for nutrient\nexchange and vesicles for storage of\nnutrients.\n• VAM produces a glue-like protein\ncalled glomalin, which helps\naggregate soil particles, improving\nsoil structure, aeration, and water",
      "POTENCY :\nPowder : 1200 IP/g.\nDosage :\nLiquid : 500ml - 1000 ml / Acre\nPowder : 3-5 Kgs / Acre\ninfiltration.\n• VAM helps protect plants against soil-\nborne pathogens and nematodes by\nstrengthening the root system.\nMode of Action:\nVAM symbiotically colonizes plant\nroots, where fungal hyphae extend far beyond\nthe nutrient depletion zone to absorb\nimmobile nutrients such as phosphorus, zinc,\niron, manganese, and water directly into plant\ncells.The hyphae create an extensive\nunderground network, increasing root surface\narea, enhancing drought tolerance, nutrient\nuptake against pathogens through a physical\nbarrier, and improving soil health.\nRecommended Crop: For All Crops\nAPPLICATION\nSoil Application\nDrip irrigation"
