      "GLUCON\n(Sugarcane)\nGluconacetobacter diazotrophicus is a\nbeneficial endophytic bacterium that lives\ninside sugarcane and fixes atmospheric\nnitrogen into ammonia to promote plant\ngrowth.\nBenefits:\n• It provides significant nitrogen to the\nplant, reducing dependence on\nnitrogen fertilizers.\n• Produces phytohormones such as\nauxins, which stimulate root growth\nand shoot growth.\n• Stimulates cell elongation, resulting in\nlonger and thicker sugarcane stems.\n• Increased plant height and internodal\nlength, which directly contributes to\nmore cane growth.",
