      "METHELO (PPFM)\n(methylobacterium Extorquens)\nMethylobacterium extorquens (Pink\nPigmented Facultative Methylotroph -\nPPFM) is a beneficial bacterium associated\nwith plant growth promotion. It colonizes\nplant surfaces and forms mutualistic\nassociations that aid in nutrient utilization\nand stress tolerance.\nBenefits:\n• Helps plants withstand abiotic\nstresses such as drought, high salinity,\nand heat by modulating ethylene\nlevels through ACC deaminase\nactivity.\n• Improves plant growth by utilizing\nmethanol emitted from plants.\n• Increases crop yield and improves\nfruit quality.",
      "POTENCY :\nLiquid : 2 × 10⁸ / ml\nDosage :\nLiquid : 500ml - 1000 ml / Acre.\n• Produces plant growth regulators like\nauxins, cytokinins, and gibberellins.\n• Improves seed germination, root\ndevelopment, and accelerates\nvegetative growth.\nMode of Action:\nMethylobacterium extorquens\ncolonizes the phyllosphere (leaf surface) and\nutilizes methanol released by plants. It\nproduces growth-promoting substances and\nACC deaminase, which helps reduce stress-\ninduced ethylene levels, enhancing plant\ngrowth and development.\nAPPLICATION\nRecommended Crops:\nFoliar Spray\nPaddy, Wheat, Vegetables,\nBanana."
